WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.033
Even a model that answers perfectly in one request can know nothing about it in the next.

2
00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:09.713
That's because a context window is a budget for one request,

3
00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:13.700
while memory is state stored outside the model and retrieved later.

4
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.933
So a chat app that seems to remember is resending earlier turns into the context each time.

5
00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:23.293
And a bigger window doesn't guarantee recall,

6
00:00:23.293 --> 00:00:25.673
because even when a long contract fits,

7
00:00:25.673 --> 00:00:28.233
a clause halfway through can still go unused.

8
00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:31.473
So I'd ask how long the information must survive,

9
00:00:31.473 --> 00:00:37.093
keeping this request's evidence in context and storing what later requests need outside the model.
